From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mackid1993 <david@brustein.net>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:15:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DirecTV: Android TV client, DAI ad insertion, and inserted-ad
 audio fixes

Signs the DirecTV source in end to end as DirecTV's own Android TV app (OAuth client UNIFIED_Android_TV_02) via its device-code grant: credential-less (approve a code once in a browser), with token refresh that re-mints the DRM activation token and self-heals a DRM 403.

Adds a per-source 'Use DirecTV ad insertion (DAI)' toggle. When on, playback uses DirecTV's Yospace ad-insertion stream (streamURL, authorized on channel/v2) instead of the fallback, with the same ad flags DirecTV's own Android TV app sends, filled from each account's own data (DMA, GPP consent -> is_lat, household/profile ids) and the playback device's ids. A viewer-profile picker runs the session as a chosen profile. Clears the playback cache when the toggle changes.

Fixes the inserted-ad audio: swaps each band-limited inserted AC-3 ad for its full-range HE-AAC twin, and attenuates the HE-AAC ad loudness about 12 dB losslessly so breaks match the programming.

The logic lives in app/scrapers/directv_dai.py, dtv_android.py, dtv_aac_ads.py and dtv_aac_gain.py; upstream files only get one-line hooks.
